{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1090253-summoning-spirits","id":1090253,"title":"Summoning Spirits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-09T05:44:56-07:00","id":1090253,"title":"Summoning Spirits","content":"So, I'm working on a setting where all magic takes the form of spirit summoning and binding. The intent being, you screw up with magic thing will go very very badly. I very much want to evoke the idea that magic is a dark and dangerous power, and when people go burning witches and whatnot that they very much have good cause to do so.<br /> <br /> But it's finals week and I've already dumped to much time into this for now, so I decided to see if the community could organize related sources to make the job easier once I have more time. If this project actually goes somewhere, obviously I'll share.<br /> <br /> So what I'm looking for is sources that describe the summoning, binding, and banishment of spirits, along with other spirit related rules for example possession, the gauntlet, etc. CoD and NWoD sources are both acceptable, I started with Inferno and it has been a wealth of information. I'd rather avoid splat specific methods unless they can be generalize for wider use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/151-hark","name":"Hark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar151_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"932"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T06:27:32-07:00","id":1090264,"title":"","content":"Second Sight has explicit rules for dealing with spirits magically, as well as for powers gained by worshiping eldritch creatures if you want to branch out from just Spirit spirits.<br /> <br /> Otherwise:<ul><li>Book of spirits is the obvious one (contains spirits, how to interact with them, and so forth).</li> <li>Predators is werewolf specific, but contains a lot of potential spirits to be summoned.</li> <li>Summoners for mage needs a bit of tinkering to generalise but shouldn't be too hard, and contains detailed rules on summoning things from various worlds.</li> <li>Most of Immortals is irrelevant, but one of the three groups are those who gain eternal youth and power from spiritual bargains.</li> <li>Mage Chroniclers guide has a (very short) section on refluffing supernal magic to be more &quot;old bargins with dark powers&quot;</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12109-urbenmyth","name":"Urbenmyth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"166"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:59:28-07:00","id":1090330,"title":"","content":"Check out the CofD 2E corebook. In the section about Ephemeral Beings it provides rules on how to summon, research, abjure, banish, and ward against any Ephemeral Being. By default, this is a thing that pretty much anyone can do (see <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/931824-so-you-want-to-be-an-exorcist\">So You Want To Be An Exorcist</a> by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1170_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1170\" data-vbnamecard=\"1170\">amechra</a> for a really good in depth look about how to do it well) but for some people it comes more easily than others. The Dark Eras book (both of them) offer great perspectives on people who truly <i>believe </i>in the kinds of creatures that live in the dark, especially in specific cultural contexts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T18:27:28-07:00","id":1090543,"title":"","content":"While not directly related to summoning spirits, Open Rites and Closed Rites from Dark Eras Companion are good for human sorcery in general and can be easily reskinned to originate from spirits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}